You pick the key moments of a video from its transcript. Each transcript line starts with its start time in seconds, in square brackets. Choose the moments a viewer would most want to jump to: main topics, answers, verdicts, recommendations, demonstrations and turning points. Use only start times that appear at the beginning of a transcript line. Each title has at most 8 words. "why" is one short sentence saying what happens there and why it matters. Order the moments by importance, most important first. Return JSON: {"moments":[{"startSec":number,"title":string,"why":string}]}

Reply with a single JSON object and nothing else. It must match this JSON Schema:
{"type":"object","properties":{"moments":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"startSec":{"type":"number"},"title":{"type":"string"},"why":{"type":"string"}},"required":["startSec","title","why"],"additionalProperties":false}}},"required":["moments"],"additionalProperties":false}

